# Window Instance Loop (mandatory)

When bound to a Window Instance (`loop_id` from wake JSON or INSTANCE.md):

## Read order (every wake)

1. `INSTANCE.md` — loop config + paste line
2. `IDENTITY.md` — role, skills, forbidden
3. `RITUAL.md` — 9-phase tick
4. Wake JSON `state_snapshot` (or `state_api get snapshot`) — **not** Read STATE.md

Use wake JSON `allowed_phase` (always `1-wake` on new tick), `read_order`, and `phase_line`.

## Strict phase line (no jumps)

Every wake **starts at Phase 1** (`1-wake`). Advance **one phase at a time** only:

`1-wake → 2-orient → 3-select → 4-execute → 5-verify → 6-review → 7-triage → 8-close → 9-arm`

**Forbidden:** jumping phases (e.g. `4-execute` → `9-arm`); setting `phase=9-arm` before `verify-wake.sh` passes; arming when `validate_ritual_gate.py` fails.

**Phase 1 first action (mandatory — before reading any file):** Run `advance_ritual_step.sh . --state-file <state_file> --loop-id <loop_id> --apply` — advances `9-arm → 1-wake` and resets per-tick flags (**never directly write `CHECKPOINT.phase`**). Until this runs, the checkpoint still shows stale `phase=9-arm` from the prior tick; the arm gate will pass immediately and skip all work. Run this **before** reading INSTANCE, IDENTITY, or STATE.

**Between ticks:** `wake=ARMED` with `phase=9-arm` is expected at rest — the arm sleeper is counting down. On a new wake, Phase 1 must call `advance_ritual_step.sh --apply` first to begin the tick and advance to `1-wake`.

After Phase 1 advances, walk the line. Phase 3: run `prepare_select_tick.sh` then `instance_worktree.sh create` when required — **cannot enter Phase 4** without active worktree (engineer/designer/qa). Phase 5: run `prepare_review_tick.sh --apply`.

## 9-phase ritual (all windows)

| Phase | Name |
|-------|------|
| 1 | Wake |
| 2 | Orient |
| 3 | Select |
| 4 | Execute |
| 5 | Verify |
| 6 | Code review |
| 7 | Receive review |
| 8 | Close |
| 9 | Arm |

**Worktree (code items):** Phase 3 runs `prepare_select_tick.sh` + creates `.worktrees/<loop_id>/`; Phases 4–7 run there; Phase 8 merges to `main` then removes worktree. See [`RITUAL.base.md`](../../docs/window-instances/_template/RITUAL.base.md).

Update `CHECKPOINT.phase` after each phase. Spec: [`docs/window-instances/_template/SPEC.md`](../../docs/window-instances/_template/SPEC.md).

## Mandatory review cycle

After Phase 5, set `CHECKPOINT.code_changed` via **window-scoped** git diff (`prepare_review_tick.sh --apply` writes `review_changed_files` + `review_fingerprint`).

Wake JSON includes `changed_files` when diff exists at wake start — **must read every listed file** before Phase 8.

| `code_changed` | Required |
|----------------|----------|
| `yes` | Phase 6 [`/code-review`](../../.cursor/commands/code-review.md) → Phase 7a Superpowers **receiving-code-review** skill + [`/receiving-code-review`](../../.cursor/commands/receiving-code-review.md) → Phase 7b backlog reflect |
| `no` | Skip with `review_status=skipped` + `review_skip_reason` |

**Round N** = `CHECKPOINT.review_round`. Phase 6 logs findings with `source=round-{N}`; Phase 7 processes only those rows.

Cannot arm (Phase 9) if `code_changed=yes` and round-N findings are untriaged.

## Phase gate (cannot skip)

**Cannot arm wake (Phase 9) if:**

- `CHECKPOINT.phase` is before `8-close`
- `CHECKPOINT.review_status` is `pending`
- `worktree_status=active` (unmerged worktree)
- `code_changed=yes` and no REVIEW_FINDINGS row with `source` containing `round-{N}`

**Allowed skip:** set `review_status=skipped` with non-empty `review_skip_reason` (docs-only ticks).

**Cannot set Phase 8 close if** `review_status=pending` unless transitioning from Phase 6/7 with explicit skip.

## REVIEW_FINDINGS (Phase 6–7)

Log findings in STATE `REVIEW_FINDINGS` table:

| id | severity | finding | source | action | backlog_ref | status |

- Id convention: `{prefix}-r{N}-{seq}` (zero-finding sentinel: `{prefix}-r{N}-000`)
- Severity: `critical` | `high` | `medium` | `low`
- Action: `fix-now` | `backlog` | `closed` | `pushback`
- Status: `open` | `closed`

Triage each round-N row in Phase 7a. Complete Phase 7b backlog reflect before Phase 8 close.

## Isolation

## State I/O (mandatory)

- **Get own state:** `bash tools/cursor-loop/scripts/state_api.sh . --loop-id <loop_id> get snapshot|checkpoint|backlog --open`
- **Set own state:** `state_api.sh ... set checkpoint field=val` / `append history` / `append review-finding` / `mark backlog-done --id X`
- **Cross-instance read:** `state_api.sh . --loop-id <caller_id> get handoff --target <other_loop_id>` (returns sections defined in HANDOFF_RULES)
- **Cross-instance write:** `state_api.sh . --loop-id <target_loop_id> append backlog-row --section <SECTION> --id <id> --row "| ... |"`
- **Forbidden:** Direct `Read` or edit of **any** `STATE.md` file at **any** phase — always use `state_api`
- Wake JSON includes `state_snapshot` — use it before any shell call

Registry: [`docs/window-instances/instances.manifest.json`](../../docs/window-instances/instances.manifest.json)  
Handoffs: each instance's `IDENTITY.md` (see manifest `handoffs_out`)

## Phase 9 delegates to agent-loop-contract

After Phase 8 close: `checkpoint-loop.py --product` + `arm-wake.sh` + `verify-wake.sh` exit 0 per [`agent-loop-contract.mdc`](agent-loop-contract.mdc).

**Steady state:** between turns, `instance-doctor` should show `wake=ARMED` for your `loop_id`. Dynamic wake is one-shot per arm — DOWN after a sentinel fires is normal mid-turn, **not** at turn end.

**Follow-up turns** ("Briefly inform…", recovery wakes): if `verify-wake` shows DOWN, re-arm before ending the turn.

Phase 9 checklist: [`docs/window-instances/_template/RITUAL.base.md`](../../docs/window-instances/_template/RITUAL.base.md).

